The function open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.refusal_phrase_in returns 'I cannot' for both Reply1 ('I can't do that. I cannot help.') and Reply2 ('I cannot help.'), even though the documented rule requires 'I can't' for Reply1 and 'I cannot' for Reply2, because it iterates over refusal phrases in list order rather than by earliest occurrence in the text.